{
 "chapter": 6,
 "title": "So how high is high enough?",
 "duration": 116.23333333333242,
 "cues": [
  {
   "start": 4.799999999999997,
   "end": 9.805487528344669,
   "text": "If waiting is worth money, why does she ever build at all? Why not wait for ever?",
   "voice": "c"
  },
  {
   "start": 10.233333333333327,
   "end": 18.043446712018135,
   "text": "Because waiting is not free. Every month she waits, she gives up a month of profit she could have been making.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 19.266666666666655,
   "end": 28.653378684807244,
   "text": "So there is some level of money coming in that is high enough that waiting any longer stops being worth it. That level has a name.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 30.200000000000042,
   "end": 37.29215419501138,
   "text": "The trigger. The level the money coming in must reach before building is actually the right thing to do.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 41.73333333333326,
   "end": 45.35464852607703,
   "text": "Here is Marshall's line again, where we left it.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 45.799999999999876,
   "end": 56.67514739229013,
   "text": "Marshall's line stays exactly where it is. It is not wrong about arithmetic. But the line where Nell should actually build slides up above it.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 57.89999999999975,
   "end": 65.78231292516982,
   "text": "And that gap has a meaning. It is the value of the chance to wait \u2014 the thing she destroys the moment she builds.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 66.99999999999969,
   "end": 74.89664399092939,
   "text": "Build now, and the chance to wait is gone for ever. She has to be paid for that, and the gap is the price.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 76.53333333333295,
   "end": 82.7110657596368,
   "text": "There is a mirror image of this on the way down, and chapter ten builds it properly.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 83.1333333333329,
   "end": 88.95578231292474,
   "text": "Marshall says: shut down when the money stops covering the day-to-day costs.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 89.39999999999951,
   "end": 99.94408163265257,
   "text": "The right answer is lower. She should absorb real losses before she gives up \u2014 because giving up throws away the chance of things getting better.",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 102.16666666666605,
   "end": 104.7315192743758,
   "text": "waiting costs forgone profit",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 104.86666666666599,
   "end": 108.00721088435307,
   "text": "a trigger: high enough to stop waiting",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 108.1333333333326,
   "end": 110.65854875283374,
   "text": "trigger above the textbook line",
   "voice": "n"
  },
  {
   "start": 110.7999999999992,
   "end": 113.87088435374069,
   "text": "and the mirror image on the way down",
   "voice": "n"
  }
 ],
